infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title What shared join keys buy you
  desc One inconsistency turns a 30-second triage into a 20-minute multi-tab search
  compares
    - label With shared join keys
      children
        - label Pivot in under 30 seconds
          desc Metric spike to log line to trace is one click chain
        - label Same names everywhere
          desc service.name, trace_id, http.route identical across all three signals
        - label Exemplar opens the exact trace
          desc Click the dot on the >1s histogram bucket; no timestamp guessing
        - label Dashboards and run-books portable
          desc OTel Semantic Conventions define the canonical field names
        - label Three backends, one surface
          desc Prometheus + Loki + Jaeger navigate as if one system
    - label Without shared join keys
      children
        - label 20-minute multi-tab search
          desc Every pivot needs manual query translation between conventions
        - label route vs http_path vs http.route
          desc Three names for one field; nothing joins automatically
        - label Guess the trace from a timestamp
          desc No exemplar bridge; wrong half the time
        - label Fragile, ad-hoc run-books
          desc Each dashboard reinvents its own naming
        - label Three disconnected dashboards
          desc No narrative across metrics, logs, and traces
